title: Commonwealth intervention of Dornwich
subtitle: History repeats itself.
view-if: not saxony_joever and (reichsex_sax_trigger or (reichsexekution_defeated = 0 and president = "DuFour" and red_saxony and (banner_force + vanguard_force < 75) and not presidential_powers and (heartland_coup_seen or heartland_reichsexekution or dufour_angry >= 100 or dufour_angry_bruning >= 50 or strife >= 5 or banner_militancy >= 0.1 or bruning_time or thuringia_joever) and year >= 1930))
on-arrival: saxony_joever = 1; strife += 1; dufour_angry += 40; dufour_angry_bruning -= 40
new-page: true
tags: event
face-image: img/Commonwealth Army.jpg

= Commonwealth intervention of Dornwich

President [+ president +] has invoked the <i>Commonwealth intervention</i> to dismiss the Dornish government, citing its "inability to maintain order" amidst escalating clashes between the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>, the Banners, and the increasingly militant <span style="color: #700000;">**Vanguard**</span>. The militarization of the <span style="color: #700000;">**Vanguard**</span> has invoked memories of what transpired years prior.

However, the true motivation is clear: the left-wing coalition governing Dornwich poses a direct threat to the conservative and nationalist establishment in the Commonwealth.

- @defend
- @surrender

@defend
title: Fight against this overthrow attempt!
subtitle: Labor will call a general strike. The the Banners and Vanguard will be mobilized to resist the Commonwealth Army. 

The Commonwealth Army and Stalhelm are already preparing to enter Dornwich. Our forces are unprepared for a fight and many Reformists think that the risk of civl war over Dornwich is too high. Do we recognize this?

- @defend_2: We will defend the Dornish Government with the Collectivists. 
- @surrender

@defend_2
on-arrival: resist_coup = 1; saxony_joever = 0; reformist_dissent += 10; defense_strength = banner_strength*banner_militancy*(1-dissent/2); defense_strength += vanguard_strength*vanguard_militancy; defense_strength += commons_marcher_normalized*(1 - dissent)*(2 - disfavored/100); defense_strength += commons_collectivist_normalized*(2 - disfavored/100); defense_strength *= 0.8; enemy_strength = loyalist_strength*loyalist_militancy + warden_strength*warden_militancy; enemy_strength += army_strength*army_militancy*(1-army_loyalty)
go-to: defend_2_civil_war if defense_strength < enemy_strength; defend_2_victory if defense_strength >= enemy_strength

@defend_2_civil_war

As the Commonwealth Army and their reactionary auxiliaries march into Dornwich, armed fighting erupts between them and the leftist forces of the Dornish government. [+ president +] refuses to withdraw the Commonwealth intervention and orders more Commonwealth Army troops into Dornwich.  

- @civil_war: It is a civil war.

@defend_2_victory
on-arrival: loyalist_strength *= 0.8; warden_strength *= 0.8; left_dissent -= 15; reformist_dissent -= 10; reichsexekution_defeated = 1; pro_republic += 5; commons_marcher += 5; disfavored_marcher += 5; commons_collectivist += 3; disfavored_collectivist += 3; commons_royalist -= 6; disfavored_royalist -= 6; dufour_angry -= 50; dufour_angry_bruning += 40; coup_victory = 1; collectivist_relation += 15; vanguard_strength += 150; vanguard_militancy += 0.1; banner_strength += 200
achievement: drei_pfeile

The the Banners and Vanguard confront the reactionaries on the road to Dornwich and somehow, the enemy has retreated without a fight! They were surprised by our resistance and [+ president +] has decided to not risk a civil war over Dornwich.

This show of force has reinvigorated support for both the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> and has weakened the Sovereigntists and reactionaries. [+ president +]'s ire has also been turned away from us. For now.

@surrender
title: Resign our positions, to prevent bloodshed.
subtitle: [+ president +] will appoint a right-wing <i>Commonwealth Commissioner</i>.
on-arrival: red_saxony = 0; commons_marcher -= 5; commons_collectivist -= 5; disfavored_collectivist -= 5; disfavored_marcher -= 5; left_dissent += 15; labor_dissent += 5; banner_militancy = banner_militancy*0.7; banner_strength -= 250; vanguard_banned = 1; vanguard_strength -= 150; vanguard_militancy -= 0.1; collectivist_relation -= 20; communist_coalition -= 1

The <span style="color: #700000;">collectivists</span> protesting in the streets are brutally suppressed, with the Commonwealth Army patrolling the streets, restricting political gatherings, and turning a blind eye to the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> as they harass local party officials.

[+ president +] appoints [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] member Dorian Brunwell as <i>Commonwealth Commissioner</i> to govern Dornwich, tasked with dismantling our reforms and violently suppressing the <span style="color: #700000;">**Vanguard**</span>.
